#====================================================================
# E600 — HMDFS setgid prevents mktemp from creating writable confstat dirs
#====================================================================

# Layer 0: Error Surface
id:                     E600
trigger_tool:           configure
phase:                  configuration
error_signature: |
  Permission denied.*confstat
  confstat.*Permission denied
  cannot create.*temporary directory

# Layer 1: Recognition
severity:               2
category:               hmdfs, build-system, portability
prescan_pattern:        umask 077.*mktemp|mktemp.*confstat
root_cause:             |
  The conan build dir (b/) on HMDFS is setgid (group=file_manager).
  The vendor configure script uses `umask 077 && mktemp -d -q ./confstatXXXXXX`.
  On HMDFS, this creates confstat dirs with mode 0270 owned by group=file_manager
  (uid 20001006), not the build user (uid 20020101).  Even though the build
  user is in the file_manager group, the setgid bit forces the result to be
  owned by file_manager, and 0270 grants no write permission to the group.
  HMDFS enforces owner-based permission checking strictly, so the build user
  cannot write to its own temp dirs.  chmod does not help because HMDFS
  enforces the permission model at the filesystem level.

# Layer 2: Fix Strategy
rec_approach:           build-in-user-owned-dir
fix_description:        |
  (a) Copy source from export_sources_folder to a fully user-owned build
  root such as /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/<name>-build.  This prevents setgid
  inheritance because the parent dir is no longer setgid.
  (b) Patch the configure script to use `umask 022` instead of `umask 077`,
  so mktemp creates dirs with mode 0755 instead of 0270.
  (c) Redirect confstat paths to the build root using `sed -i` in the
  recipe's build() method.
  (d) Run configure/make/install from the build script (do_build.sh) with
  the conan environment (conanbuild.sh) properly sourced.

fix_code:               |
  # In conanfile.py build() method:
  import subprocess
  build_root = "/storage/Users/currentUser/usr/nylon-build"
  if os.path.exists(build_root):
      shutil.rmtree(build_root)
  os.makedirs(build_root, 0o755)
  # Copy source...
  # Patch configure:
  subprocess.run([
      "sed", "-i",
      "-e", "s|(umask 077|(umask 022|g",
      "-e", "s|./confstat$$-|%s/confstat$$-|g" % build_root,
      "-e", "s|./confstatXXXXXX|%s/confstatXXXXXX|g" % build_root,
      os.path.join(build_root, "configure"),
  ], check=True)

fix_reference:           archives/n/nylon/1.21/conanfile.py (nylon 1.21)

# Layer 3: Validation
validation:             |
  - Source tree copied to /storage/Users/currentUser/usr/<name>-build (verified by
    stat that the dir is owned by uid 20020101, not setgid).
  - configure completes without "Permission denied" errors in config.status.
  - make completes without "Permission denied" errors in the temp file operations.
